    {
      "template_id": "text",
      "color_scheme": "light",
      "content": {
        "text_elements": [
          {
            "template_id": "subtitle_small",
            "content": {
              "text": "OnStove 工具"
            }
          },
          {
            "template_id": "paragraph_medium",
            "content": {
              "text": "[needs translation] Open-source clean cooking geospatial models such as the <a href=\"https://github.com/Open-Source-Spatial-Clean-Cooking-Tool/OnStove\"><u>OnStove Tool</u></a> deployed in Nepal integrate cost-benefit analysis to determine the most beneficial fuel-stove alternative for specific communities (<a href=\"https://www.wri.org/update/energy-access-explorer-open-software-enabling-access-clean-cooking-nepal\"><u>WRI, 2023</u></a>).<br /><br />OnStove uses high-resolution spatial data to calculate the net benefit of various cooking technologies by comparing four key benefits: reduced morbidity, mortality, time saved, and emissions avoided, against three cost dimensions: capital, fuel, and operations and maintenance.<br /><br />By overlaying these metrics on demographic, infrastructure, and energy maps, the tool allows users, to assess where clean cooking solutions offer the greatest socio-economic and environmental benefits. OnStove 可以帮助解决关键数据缺口，并支持基于证据的决策，以扩大清洁烹饪的覆盖范围，特别是在服务不足、偏远和农村地区。"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "template_id": "text",
      "color_scheme": "light",
      "content": {
        "text_elements": [
          {
            "template_id": "subtitle_small",
            "content": {
              "text": "<strong>能源获取探索器</strong>"
            }
          },
          {
            "template_id": "paragraph_medium",
            "content": {
              "text": "<a href=\"https://www.energyaccessexplorer.org/tool/a/?id=5d137d39-e46d-4abc-bfc9-76254501fa09&output=eai&view=inputs&variant=raster&tab=controls&divtier=0&subdiv=0\"><u>Energy Access Explorer</u></a> 是一个开源的在线地理空间平台，旨在为能源规划者、清洁能源创业者、捐助者和发展机构提供服务。 它帮助用户识别能源获取干预的优先领域。 它还作为一个信息系统，简化数据管理和治理，同时降低数据提供者和用户的成本（请参见下面的截图）。 <br /><br />EAE 既是一个规划工具，也是一个数据治理系统，减少了对复杂软件工程的需求，同时简化了数据的收集、协调和共享。 用户可以探索电网扩展、离网解决方案和可再生能源部署的机会，并评估在哪些投资或政策干预中会产生最大影响。<br /><br />"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
